    "details": "The Jackson project reports:\n\n> CVE-2026-89407: NumberInput.looksLikeValidNumber() pre-validates\n> stringified numbers with PATTERN_FLOAT, whose adjacent quantifiers\n> allow catastrophic backtracking on crafted input.\n>\n> CVE-2026-89425: UTF8DataInputJsonParser builds the offending token\n> text for an error message in a loop without an upper bound, so it\n> ignores maxErrorTokenLength. The other three parser implementations\n> are not affected.\n",
